GRC AI Agent
Software Design Document
04-25-2026
Team AI Agent
Alp Berrak and Carter Jules
































Executive Summary

The Automated GRC AI Agent streamlines risk assessments and identifies applicable data-privacy regulations for organizations in the business and finance sector. The agent is implemented as an n8n workflow triggered from Slack. The workflow collects structured inputs (location, sector, states, user volume, and self-evaluation of system subsections) and executes three AI Agent nodes and uses Retrieval-Augmented Generation to pull supplemental information for the AI Agents to use from a GitHub. The supplemental information includes data privacy regulations and NIST recommendations formatted as JSONs for easy parsing and appending. The result is a concise, readable report returned to users via Slack DMs that reduces hallucination risk by constraining agents to the supplemental information provided by vector store tools.

Current limitations include scope restricted to the business/finance sector, recommendation sourcing limited to NIST SP 800-53, and dependency on timely updates to the curated GitHub vector stores and quality of user self-evaluations. Planned enhancements are sector-specific vector stores, broader recommendation sources (industry best practices, vendor controls), automated regulatory updates, and expanded UI integrations beyond Slack. Together, these elements position the GRC AI Agent as an efficient, auditable first-pass compliance tool with clear paths for scaling coverage and depth.
Business Purpose and Statement
Our GRC AI Agent assists organizations in conducting risk assessments of their system configurations. It can be used as a way to automate the risk assessment process, and alleviate the burden of determining what data privacy regulations are required to comply with

The landscape of data privacy regulations is constantly changing, and noncompliance results in hefty fines that severely financially impact an organization. Our system is able to quickly determine which regulations apply to an organization, saving employees significant time while helping to avoid paying substantial fines.

Additionally, risk assessments of a system configuration can often be time consuming and complex. By using our system, users are able to begin the risk assessment process by self evaluating their system configuration and receiving up to date recommendations following NIST cybersecurity standards, therefore providing a starting point for system upgrades. This is an efficient way to eliminate some of the grunt work in risk assessments, and provide an overview of possible upgrades to an organization.

Risk assessments are crucial when handling sensitive personal data of your users or consumers. Users of an organization put trust into it by providing personal data, and that sense of trust is necessary for an organization to operate at its best. Our system enables organizations to conduct efficient risk assessments and receive upgrade options in order to retain user trust and prevent data breaches and cyber attacks
Intended Audience
As the scope of our AI Agent is limited to the business and finance sector, the intended audience for our system is organizations who operate under that sector. Data privacy regulations vary from sector to sector within the US, so currently the AI Agent is equipped to determine what regulations an organization must follow under Federal Data Privacy Regulations that apply strictly to financial or business data. 

Although the scope was limited based on the patch work legislation for data privacy within the United States, this AI Agent is able to be utilized by global companies. Our system can determine which International Data Privacy regulations an organization must follow, as well as state specific data privacy regulations for organizations located in the US. 

On a user level, the AI Agent can be used by those with a base level understanding of a system configuration. Because “I don’t know” is a valid answer to the self evaluation form, employees of an organization who may not have access to system configuration plans are still able to utilize the service and receive possible upgrades for a system regardless of what they know. The only barrier to using the AI Agent is an understanding of what each subsection in the of the self evaluation form means in terms of system configurations (e.g what Identity and Asset Management is). 
